# Wave W17-V (Route 207): climb turf — foothill turf with ring-glint flecks: a bright climbing green carrying sparse pale-gold glints, the design’s scattered RELICT rings catching the sun in the grass (design: the road climbs the whole way; relic rings lie in the foothill grass). Route 207’s own ground — split from Route 203’s smoke-greyed coal turf by the glints and the brightness (treasure in the grass vs dust on it) and from Route 208’s warm rest meadow by register (the climb strains, the rest road breathes).
